tion: The hand 6 of Hearts and 10 of Clubs (10-6 offsuit) is a statistically weak hand with very low playability. It lacks connectivity for straights, is not suited for flushes, and has low high-card value. Facing a raise from the opponent indicates they likely have a stronger range. Calling would require investing more chips into a pot where you are significantly behind in equity, and raising as a bluff is ill-advised with such a weak holding and deep stacks.\n\nReason: Due to the poor strength of the hand and the aggression shown by the opponent, the Expected Value (EV) of continuing is negative. Folding minimizes losses and preserves the chip stack for hands with better winning potential.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
