ike AJ+), ATs is often dominated or flipping at best. We need nearly 50% equity to justify the call, and against a strong range, we likely have 30-40%. Unless the opponent is bluffing wildly, this is negative expected value.\n\nReason: Calling a 100BB all-in with Ace-Ten suited is statistically a losing play against a standard opponent range consisting of pairs and stronger Aces. Preserving the chip stack for a better opportunity is the prudent move.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
